Synchronize GPU-painted tiles across GL contexts

The compositor and the Skia painting threads share pooled GL textures across
contexts without fences; Mali-G310 then runs their GPU work out of order and
tiles show old pixels. Painted tiles are copied, painting targets (tiles and
scrollbars) are pooled apart from the compositor's textures, and a texture's
next writer waits for its last reader (or the work finishes when no fence can
be made).

